# ResinCompute development + CI dependencies.
#
# Runtime deps are deliberately empty - see requirements.txt. Nothing pinned
# here may be imported by shipped code; ruff, pytest and mypy exist to lint,
# test and type-check it, and pytest-timeout is a pytest plugin (slice 0i(4b),
# DECISION B, docs/LEDGER.md; pytest-xdist and execnet are deferred there).
# tests/test_dev_pin_declaration.py lists plugins in PLUGINS, because no gate
# invokes a plugin by name.
#
# Pinned with == rather than >=. CI installs these (via the compiled
# requirements-dev.txt) on every run, and an
# unpinned lint tool means a new ruff release can turn the tree red on a commit
# that changed nothing. Bump these deliberately, in their own commit, so the
# diff that introduces new findings is the diff that raised the pin.
#
# Versions below were resolved and installed on 2026-09-06.
#
# LAYOUT (MAIN ORDER 0300, 2026-10-05): this .in file is the HUMAN-EDITED
# declaration - which tools, at which `==` version. requirements-dev.txt is
# GENERATED from it by pip-compile with --generate-hashes: the full transitive
# closure with a sha256 for every distribution, installed in CI with
# `pip install --require-hashes`. tests/test_dev_pin_declaration.py grades THIS
# file; tests/test_supply_chain.py grades the compiled one.
#
# Dependabot's pip updater recognises the pair (an .in next to a .txt whose
# header says "autogenerated by pip-compile"), bumps the pin here and
# re-runs pip-compile with --generate-hashes, so pins and hashes move together
# in one PR. Regenerate by hand after editing this file, from the repo root,
# with pip-tools under Python 3.11 (the header's Python version is what
# Dependabot resolves with):
#
#   python -m piptools compile --generate-hashes --strip-extras --output-file=requirements-dev.txt requirements-dev.in
#
# (One line on purpose, so it pastes into any shell without a continuation.)
#
# The generated header reads `--no-index` although that flag is NOT passed.
# pip-tools 7.5.3 writes it itself (measured 2026-10-10: the command above,
# run under Python 3.11 with network access, emits that exact header). Do not
# add --no-index to the command - it would make pip ignore PyPI and resolve
# nothing.
#
# colorama: pip-compile drops pytest's `sys_platform == "win32"` marker, and a
# Linux recompile (Dependabot) drops colorama entirely. After recompiling,
# restore the line `colorama==0.4.6 ; sys_platform == "win32"` by hand so
# Windows dev installs keep working.
#
# Do not hand-edit requirements-dev.txt: Dependabot overwrites it whole.

ruff==0.16.10
pytest==9.1.1
mypy==2.4.0
pytest-timeout==2.4.0
